<%# Port of the legacy SPA `Hujah/card_small.js` — a threaded child response. The left border
    is colored by the responder's stance, and the element is a response-filter item
    tagged with that stance so the Stimulus filter can show/hide it.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.3) —
    docs/design-system/components/hujah/CompactHujahCard.prompt.md: "the 8px left border
    is the responder's stance — this is the signature Hoojah motif. Tallies below the
    body are faint light-grey, all three stances always shown."

    That border now comes from `ui/_card`'s `stance:` rather than from interpolating the
    stance into `border-<...>` here. The interpolation LOOKED harmless — every stance is
    in the `@source inline` safelist — but it had no guard: `ds_card_classes` raises on a
    value outside CARD_STANCES, whereas raw interpolation of a typo yields a class with no
    rule behind it and renders as a card that merely looks unstanced. Neither review nor
    CI sees that. The `|| "primary"` fallback for an unvoted response is in the set for
    exactly this reason.

    `padded:` stays unset (the inner rows own their padding) and `pr-2 flex items-center
    mb-1` rides in `class:`. `mb-1` is 4px, not the feed's 8px, deliberately: the
    challenge row below hangs off it with `-mt-1`, and threaded children stack tighter
    than top-level cards.

    FROZEN: `data-response-filter-target="item"` / `data-response-filter-vote` are the
    response-filter controller's whole API and are matched by string against the copies
    documented in `_response_filter` and repeated in `_challenge_dialog`. They stay on
    the anchor, spelled exactly as they were. %>
<% stance = {1 => "agree", 2 => "neutral", 3 => "disagree"}[child.vote] || "primary" %>
<%= link_to hujah_path(child.slug),
      class: "block no-underline",
      data: { "response-filter-target": "item", "response-filter-vote": stance } do %>
  <%= render layout: "ui/card",
        locals: {stance: stance, class: "pr-2 flex items-center mb-1"} do %>
    <div class="flex py-1">
      <%# 32px — the design system's compact-card avatar. Via the partial because
          `image_tag user.photo` raises on a photoless responder and would take the
          whole thread down with it. %>
      <%= render "ui/avatar", user: child.user, size: :sm, class: "mx-2" %>
      <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
        <div>
          <span class="mr-1 text-primary"><%= child.user.full_name %></span>
          <small class="text-sm text-grey">@<%= child.user.username %></small>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-0 text-black break-words"><%= format_body(child.body) %></div>
        <div class="flex items-center text-sm text-light-grey fill-light-grey">
          <%= stance_icon("agree", class: "w-4 h-4") %><span class="ml-1"><%= child.agree_count.to_i %></span>
          <span class="mx-2">·</span>
          <%= stance_icon("neutral", class: "w-4 h-4") %><span class="ml-1"><%= child.neutral_count.to_i %></span>
          <span class="mx-2">·</span>
          <%= stance_icon("disagree", class: "w-4 h-4") %><span class="ml-1"><%= child.disagree_count.to_i %></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<%# "Challenge to debate" escalates this argument into a one-on-one debate. Shown
    only to a signed-in viewer who is not the argument's author. Rendered OUTSIDE the
    card anchor (a <dialog>/<form> can't nest in an <a>) — CompactHujahCard.prompt.md
    says the same thing about `ChallengeLink`: "renders below the card, never inside it".
    It carries the same response-filter item+vote so it hides in sync with the card. %>
<% if user_signed_in? && current_user.id != child.user_id %>
  <%= render "hujahs/challenge_dialog", argument: child, hujah: hujah, stance: stance %>
<% end %>
